      "text": "April 6, 2026 | Natural Disasters Summary\n\nJarablus, Aleppo Governorate | Syria - Lightning strike killed a shepherd; heavy rain caused flooding, infrastructure damage, and evacuations.\n\nSalvatierra, Guanajuato | Mexico - Floodwaters up to 1.5 m inundated streets and swept away vehicles after intense rainfall.\n\nBolangir, Odisha | India - Severe storm with hail and winds up to 87 km/h damaged homes, crops, and killed 2 people by lightning.\n\nBogo, Cebu Province | Philippines - M5.1 earthquake injured 4 people, caused minor damage, and triggered aftershocks.\n\nApril 6-7, 2026 \n\nIslamabad, Lahore | Pakistan - Ongoing storms and heavy rain caused flooding, damage, and casualties across multiple regions.\n\nLviv, Volyn, Odesa | Ukraine - Severe weather with hail, strong winds, snow, and power outages caused widespread disruption.\n\nDerbent District | Russia - Floods and landslides killed 7 people, destroyed infrastructure, and forced thousands to evacuate.\n\nGrodno, Brest | Belarus - Cyclone Rapunzel brought hail, strong winds, fallen trees, and infrastructure damage.\n\nViti Levu | Fiji - Tropical Cyclone Waianu (Category 3) caused major power outages, flooding, and infrastructure damage.\n\n#Flooding #Storm #Cyclone #Landslide #ExtremeWeather #NaturalDisaster #ClimateEvents #GlobalWeather #EarthNews",
